            <ArticleTitle>Which factors influence the development of GVHD in HLA-matched or mismatched transplants?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>333-335</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1521-6926(17)30031-2</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.beha.2017.09.003</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The sheer diversity of HLA alleles makes the probability of finding matched unrelated donors for patients requiring hematopoietic cell transplantation (HCT) a complex situation. New evidence suggests that mismatching at certain HLA loci may provide a greater benefit in terms of graft-versus-leukemia effect than other mismatches when HLA-matched donors are not available. This review summarizes the current understanding of HLA matching requirements for unrelated donor HCT.</AbstractText>
